  "query_preview": "..\n(This afternoon through Thursday)\nIssued at 1227 PM CST FRI NOV 27 2026\n\nDry and cool conditions will persist through Saturday as drier\nair remains in place. Clear skies tonight will allow temperatures\nto fall into the mid-20s across the northern half of the area by\nSaturday morning, with upper 20s to lower 30s farther south.\nTemperatures will moderate Saturday afternoon as winds shift back\nto the south, bringing increasing moisture ahead of the next\nsystem. Confidence is increasing that most of the rain will hold\noff until after sunrise Sunday. An upper-level system and\nassociated cold front will move through Sunday into early Monday,\nbringing medium to high rain chances. A few rumbles of thunder\ncan't be ruled out Sunday, but the thunderstorm threat remains\nlow due to limited instability. Drier and cooler weather returns\nearly next week as high pressure builds back in behind the front.\n\n16",
